title: Moscow's Money
new-page: true
view-if: crisis = 0 and c_subsidy_timer <= 0 and comintern_member = 1
on-arrival: c_subsidy_timer = 6; month_actions += 1
frequency: 200
is-card: true
tags: international

= Moscow's Money

The Executive's treasurer has come to Berlin with the accounts. [? if moscow_subsidy > 0 : Moscow already pays the party [+ moscow_subsidy +] funds a month, for the papers, the full-time organisers and things the accounts do not name. ?][? if moscow_subsidy = 0 : Moscow is offering a regular subsidy, for the papers, the full-time organisers and things the accounts would not name. ?] [? if year >= 1921 and year <= 1922 : The money comes from a country where people are starving. ?]

Money from Moscow keeps the party alive. It also means Moscow's voice weighs more at every Central Committee meeting.

- @more: Accept a larger regular subsidy.
- @accounts: Take a one-off payment, and keep our own accounts.
- @refuse: Live on our own dues.
- @easy_discard

@more
subtitle: More funds every month. Our independence suffers.
choose-if: moscow_subsidy < 2
unavailable-subtitle: Moscow will not pay more than it does.
on-arrival: moscow_subsidy += 1; independence -= 10; offensive_satisfaction += 3; luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 4; lean_offensive += 1

The money will arrive every month through a bank in Stockholm. So will the letters from the Executive.

@accounts
subtitle: 1 fund. The treasurer is not pleased with our bookkeeping.
on-arrival: resources += 1; independence += 2; lean_luxemburgist += 1

We take the money and send back a receipt. We do not send the minutes.

@refuse
subtitle: [? if moscow_subsidy > 0 : Less money each month. ?] Our independence grows; the Spartacists are proud, the Left uneasy.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.moscow_subsidy > 0) {
    Q.moscow_subsidy -= 1;
    Q.independence += 8;
} else {
    Q.independence += 4;
}
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 5;
Q.offensive_satisfaction -= 3;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
!}

A party that cannot pay for its own paper, the Zentrale writes, will not be able to make its own revolution.
